Third-party attribution:

  * stealth/payload.js draws on patterns from h4ckf0r0day/obscura
    (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/h4ckf0r0day/obscura) — specifically the
    Function.prototype.toString masking strategy, per-session deterministic
    fingerprint seed, GPU/screen pools, and Intl.DateTimeFormat wrap.
    Reimplemented for real Chrome (Object.defineProperty patches over an
    existing browser, not a from-scratch JS environment).

  * stealth/tracker_domains.txt is a copy of obscura's pgl_domains.txt
    (Apache-2.0, derived from the Peter Lowe ad/tracker host file).

  * driver/aria.py and stealth/humanizer.py adapt design patterns from
    Huzy85/fantoma (MIT) — accessibility-tree-first interaction model and
    Killourhy-Maxion key-pair classification.

  * server.py mirrors the FastMCP tool-surface convention used by
    vibheksoni/stealth-browser-mcp (MIT).
